# Digital Luggage Tags — Workspace Context

## Workspace layout

The workspace root **is** the GitHub Pages repo (deem0u.github.io). Live at https://deem0u.github.io/

- **`admin/index.html`** — Admin dashboard (manage users, keys, edit any page)
- **`edit/index.html`** — Self-service editor (users update their contact page via unique link)
- **`styles.css`** — Shared styles for admin and edit
- **`user/<username>/<contactpagename>.html`** — Per-user contact pages (e.g. `user/danielmounnarath/index.html`)
- **`cloudflare-worker/`** — API backend (Worker + wrangler). Deploy to Cloudflare Workers.
- **`release/`** — Packaged deployable artifacts (`digital-luggage-tags-artifacts.zip`)
- **`SETUP-GUIDE.md`** — Setup, daily usage, troubleshooting

## Recent modifications (repository)

- **Additional Information (optional)** — New free-text field on all contact forms:
  - Admin: New User form and Edit Contact form (`admin/index.html`)
  - Self-service: Edit form (`edit/index.html`)
  - Live contact page: New row after "Destination Details" (EN: "Additional Information", ZH: "补充信息"). Uses `.form-textarea`, `.form-label-optional`, existing CSS.
- **Admin Dashboard** — Recovery cluster on its own row; Contact Page cluster has a searchable dropdown for contact cards per user; Worker `GET /api/contact-pages/:username` lists pages for a user.
- **SETUP-GUIDE.md** — Updated with Additional Information feature, editing notes, and deploy file list.
- **Artifacts** — `release/digital-luggage-tags-artifacts.zip` includes SETUP-GUIDE, worker, wrangler, styles, admin and edit HTML.

## Deploy mapping

| Local path | Deploy target |
|------------|---------------|
| `admin/index.html` | `deem0u.github.io` repo → `admin/index.html` |
| `edit/index.html` | `edit/index.html` |
| `styles.css` | `styles.css` |
| `cloudflare-worker/worker.js` | Cloudflare Worker `contact-page-editor` |

## Git and push

- **Pull:** From workspace root: `git pull`.
- **Push:** From workspace root: `git push`. The workspace root and the remote are the same repo (deem0u.github.io).
